 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "yul-evm-compiler",
  "excerpt": "A **verified non-optimizing compiler for a fragment of Yul to EVM bytecode**, written in Lean 4. \"Non-optimizing\" describes the *core*: code generation is direct and its correctness never depends on any optimization. Two separately verified optimizers do run in front of and below it — a Yul→Yul pipeline (`Optimizer/`) and an Asm→Asm peephole (`AsmPeephole.lean`), each with its own soundness contract composed into the end-to-end theorem. See **Optimization** below."
 },
